cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Data Center Capacity Decision Model"
abstract: >-
  A stylized quantitative decision model for allocating required electrical
  capacity across candidate data-center sites when power is delivered in
  stages and its timing is uncertain. Limited, ordinal site knowledge is
  resolved through explicit published mappings into phased power-delivery
  profiles and finite delay distributions; the engine then evaluates
  allocations by exact enumeration of the joint delay space (or seeded
  Monte Carlo when that space is large), scoring each against development
  cost and the expected delay burden under the objective
  J = C_dev + lambda * E[L]. For one to three candidate sites the allocation
  is optimized exactly as a linear program; for four to twelve sites the
  application compares defined benchmark strategies and reports the best
  among them. Inputs and worked examples are synthetic and stylized.
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
license: Apache-2.0
